# Sessions

## Framework semantics

CakePHP configures sessions in `config/app.php` and exposes them via the request (`getSession()`). Cookies are set/read through response/request APIs. Prefer framework session/cookie helpers over inventing parallel PHP `$_SESSION` sprawl in app code.

## Required behavior

- Configure session engine/timeouts in config — not hardcoded in controllers.
- Prefer `$request->getSession()` over raw `$_SESSION` in application code.
- Keep flash messages via Flash component/helper patterns the project already uses.
- Set cookie flags (Secure/HttpOnly/SameSite) appropriately for the deployment.
- Do not store secrets or large blobs in session without cause.

## Anti-patterns

- Ad-hoc `$_SESSION` / `setcookie` bypassing CakePHP APIs without reason
- Session fixation-prone custom auth storage when Authentication plugin exists
- Putting authorization decisions only in session flags without server checks

## Review checklist

- [ ] Session config lives in config
- [ ] Controllers use request session/Flash conventions
- [ ] Cookie security flags match environment
